WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.211 --> 00:00:17.032
stared at her phone in shock.

2
00:00:17.712 --> 00:00:19.693
Who had sent her this mean text?

3
00:00:20.373 --> 00:00:21.933
Girls can't coach.

4
00:00:22.533 --> 00:00:24.374
Especially oafs like u.

5
00:00:24.394 --> 00:00:27.475
A player who hated her, obviously.

6
00:00:28.155 --> 00:00:30.176
She glanced uneasily around the gym.

7
00:00:31.036 --> 00:00:37.131
It was empty, except for two janitors, who were sweeping, and Marv, who was locking up the equipment

8
00:00:37.171 --> 00:00:43.734
closet. Brooklyn pulled back her shoulders.

9
00:00:44.315 --> 00:00:48.957
An elementary school teacher had once taught Brooklyn's class how to handle bullies.

10
00:00:50.138 --> 00:00:53.880
One thing Brooklyn remembered was to never let bullies bother you.

11
00:00:54.881 --> 00:00:58.683
And if they did bother you, you were supposed to talk to an adult about it.

12
00:00:58.703 --> 00:01:00.224
"Take that!"

13
00:01:01.324 --> 00:01:03.286
Brooklyn pressed Delete on her phone.

14
00:01:04.227 --> 00:01:05.688
She instantly felt better.

15
00:01:07.409 --> 00:01:16.116
But at school on Monday, Brooklyn found a note folded up inside her locker: You're no coach!

16
00:01:17.217 --> 00:01:24.363
On Tuesday there was another note in her lunch bag: We need a real coach.

17
00:01:24.983 --> 00:01:26.164
Not you.

18
00:01:27.465 --> 00:01:34.853
On Wednesday she found one in her gym bag: Leave the Whales.

19
00:01:35.714 --> 00:01:42.599
On Thursday a note lay inside her history book: Quit or the team will lose.

20
00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:45.682
Brooklyn kept the messages to herself.

21
00:01:46.322 --> 00:01:49.645
But on Friday she pulled Jacey aside before math class.

22
00:01:53.688 --> 00:02:00.934
She showed her the latest note, found in her backpack that morning: Oafs don't coach.

23
00:02:01.855 --> 00:02:03.176
Jacey's eyes widened.

24
00:02:03.864 --> 00:02:05.085
"That's so mean."

25
00:02:05.105 --> 00:02:08.368
"It's not the first message I've gotten this week."

26
00:02:08.888 --> 00:02:11.270
Brooklyn told her friend about the other messages.

27
00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:13.893
"Have you told anyone?"

28
00:02:14.333 --> 00:02:15.094
Jacey asked.

29
00:02:16.194 --> 00:02:17.295
Brooklyn shook her head.

30
00:02:17.315 --> 00:02:21.599
"The final game is coming up, so I didn't want to get anyone in trouble.

31
00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:24.201
Do you think Dirk wrote these notes?"

32
00:02:25.382 --> 00:02:26.223
Jacey shrugged.

33
00:02:26.243 --> 00:02:29.265
"I know Dirk was mad about being benched."

34
00:02:30.346 --> 00:02:34.040
"That was his fault, not mine," Brooklyn said as the bell rang.

35
00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:38.402
"We'll talk more at practice," she said quickly.

36
00:02:39.282 --> 00:02:42.323
But Brooklyn didn't get a chance to talk to Jacey at practice.

37
00:02:43.283 --> 00:02:48.464
Instead she spent almost the entire session walking around school searching for Dirk.

38
00:02:51.145 --> 00:02:54.466
Someone said they saw him in the office, so she checked there.

39
00:02:56.167 --> 00:02:56.767
No Dirk.

40
00:02:57.727 --> 00:02:59.668
Someone else claimed he was in the library.

41
00:03:00.368 --> 00:03:00.988
No Dirk.

42
00:03:02.764 --> 00:03:06.046
This was their last practice before the play-off game on Saturday.

43
00:03:07.167 --> 00:03:11.691
While Marv led the team through the loop play, Brooklyn used the phone in the gym office.

44
00:03:16.774 --> 00:03:20.917
She called Dirk's cell phone and his home, but no one answered either number.

45
00:03:23.879 --> 00:03:28.603
When Brooklyn went to tell Marv the news, she heard Jacey laughing out in the hall at the

46
00:03:28.643 --> 00:03:29.423
water fountain.

47
00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:34.442
"She wants to be a professional coach!"

48
00:03:35.363 --> 00:03:37.885
"Really?" Stuart laughed.

49
00:03:37.905 --> 00:03:40.868
"Can you coach if you don't even play?"

50
00:03:41.348 --> 00:03:41.988
Aaron asked.

51
00:03:42.008 --> 00:03:44.851
"Brooklyn wants to," said Jacey.

52
00:03:44.871 --> 00:03:46.852
"It's her big dream."

53
00:03:48.554 --> 00:03:50.696
Brooklyn hurried away before they spotted her.

54
00:03:50.716 --> 00:03:57.621
"I can't believe Jacey told them about my dream of coaching," she thought.

55
00:03:58.902 --> 00:04:00.364
Tears stung her eyes.

56
00:04:01.172 --> 00:04:05.374
It was the truth, but the way Jacey had said it made Brooklyn feel silly.

57
00:04:06.355 --> 00:04:08.376
Were Aaron and Stuart laughing at her?

58
00:04:09.057 --> 00:04:11.758
She blinked quickly to keep her tears from spilling.

59
00:04:12.839 --> 00:04:15.620
Outside the gym Brooklyn took a few deep breaths.

60
00:04:23.225 --> 00:04:24.465
She had to calm down.

61
00:04:25.746 --> 00:04:27.307
The team had had a great season.

62
00:04:27.967 --> 00:04:31.009
And if things went well, they could be league champions.

63
00:04:32.050 --> 00:04:36.473
She squared her shoulders and stepped onto the basketball court next to Marv.

64
00:04:36.493 --> 00:04:40.195
"What's next, Coach?"

65
00:04:41.696 --> 00:04:44.138
After practice Brooklyn put away the equipment.

66
00:04:46.419 --> 00:04:47.320
Marv looked at her.

67
00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:50.582
"You were awfully quiet today," he said.

68
00:04:50.602 --> 00:04:54.725
"I was worried about um, the final game.

69
00:04:55.445 --> 00:04:56.126
And Dirk."

70
00:04:56.146 --> 00:04:59.208
"We'll be fine," Marv said grimly.

71
00:04:59.976 --> 00:05:01.578
"With or without Dirk."

72
00:05:02.538 --> 00:05:07.623
When Brooklyn reached her house thirty minutes later, she was surprised to see Dirk sitting on her front

73
00:05:07.683 --> 00:05:09.545
steps holding a basketball.

74
00:05:09.565 --> 00:05:11.226
"Where were you?"

75
00:05:11.646 --> 00:05:12.727
Brooklyn demanded.

76
00:05:12.747 --> 00:05:15.870
"Today's final practice was super important."

77
00:05:15.890 --> 00:05:19.453
"I went to talk to Coach Teagan," Dirk said.

78
00:05:19.473 --> 00:05:21.095
"About the team.

79
00:05:21.975 --> 00:05:24.798
And after talking to you, I'm going to talk to Marv."

80
00:05:25.659 --> 00:05:26.940
Dirk took a big breath.

81
00:05:29.252 --> 00:05:33.054
"I didn't like you giving us plays, but you do seem to know your stuff.

82
00:05:34.095 --> 00:05:37.036
I know I haven't been a team player, and I'm sorry."

83
00:05:38.717 --> 00:05:42.219
Brooklyn was proud to hear Dirk say she knew her stuff with basketball.

84
00:05:42.239 --> 00:05:44.200
"It's okay," she said.

85
00:05:44.220 --> 00:05:46.602
"Thanks. And don't worry.

86
00:05:47.182 --> 00:05:48.903
I didn't let those notes bother me."

87
00:05:50.324 --> 00:05:51.765
Dirk frowned, confused.

88
00:05:51.785 --> 00:05:53.105
"What notes?"

89
00:05:53.726 --> 00:05:55.026
Brooklyn studied his face.

90
00:05:55.046 --> 00:05:57.568
"You didn't leave mean notes for me?

91
00:05:58.248 --> 00:05:59.168
Or text me?"

92
00:06:00.329 --> 00:06:01.289
Dirk shook his head.

93
00:06:01.309 --> 00:06:03.269
"That's creepy, Brooklyn.

94
00:06:03.790 --> 00:06:05.250
I'd never do something like that."

95
00:06:05.270 --> 00:06:09.211
"If it wasn't you Brooklyn began.

96
00:06:09.231 --> 00:06:11.112
"What do the notes say?"

97
00:06:11.612 --> 00:06:12.252
Dirk asked.

98
00:06:13.432 --> 00:06:15.693
"Uh never mind," she said quickly.

99
00:06:16.213 --> 00:06:19.394
She was still worried about upsetting the team before the final game.

100
00:06:19.414 --> 00:06:25.596
"Anyway, Marv said you'll have to sit out for the first quarter of tomorrow's game because you missed

101
00:06:25.656 --> 00:06:29.853
practice. But the Whales still need you for the other three quarters."

102
00:06:31.134 --> 00:06:34.195
Dirk stood up straighter, but he didn't respond to Brooklyn.

103
00:06:36.116 --> 00:06:38.637
He took a one-handed shot over Brooklyn's head.

104
00:06:40.358 --> 00:06:42.839
The ball swooshed through the basket over the garage.

105
00:06:42.859 --> 00:06:46.880
"Nice shot," Brooklyn said.

106
00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:52.462
Dirk had a lousy attitude sometimes, but he was definitely their team's best player.

107
00:06:53.623 --> 00:06:55.904
Dirk scooped up the ball and looked at Brooklyn.

108
00:06:56.992 --> 00:07:01.115
"Coach said I'd better step up for the team and stop being Dirk the Jerk.

109
00:07:01.616 --> 00:07:05.679
Catch!" he said, suddenly tossing the ball at her.

110
00:07:05.699 --> 00:07:11.924
"Hey!" Brooklyn laughed as the ball bounced past her.

111
00:07:11.944 --> 00:07:15.867
"Is that revenge for my giving you a black eye?"

112
00:07:15.887 --> 00:07:21.552
"Yep." Brooklyn got the ball and started dribbling in the driveway.

113
00:07:24.256 --> 00:07:27.597
She and Dirk practiced some passes and quick shots into the basket.

114
00:07:32.139 --> 00:07:33.560
Then Brooklyn stopped playing.

115
00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:35.741
"Don't you love basketball?"

116
00:07:35.761 --> 00:07:38.482
"Coach Teagan asked me the same question."

117
00:07:39.062 --> 00:07:39.843
Dirk swallowed.

118
00:07:39.863 --> 00:07:44.925
"Playing basketball makes me happier than anything else in the world."

119
00:07:44.945 --> 00:07:47.326
"I guess I'm thinking like a coach."

120
00:07:47.766 --> 00:07:48.566
Brooklyn grinned.

121
00:07:48.586 --> 00:07:52.648
"I know some Whales don't like that I'm helping Marv, right?"

122
00:07:53.384 --> 00:07:54.144
Dirk nodded.

123
00:07:54.164 --> 00:07:57.005
"No matter what, I'm not going to quit.

124
00:07:57.685 --> 00:08:02.147
There's just one more game left, and I'm sure I can help our team win the championship.

125
00:08:03.127 --> 00:08:06.028
Besides, the end-of-the-season party is at my house!"

126
00:08:07.008 --> 00:08:09.669
Brooklyn tossed Dirk the basketball, which he caught.

127
00:08:13.790 --> 00:08:15.590
Dirk spun the ball on one finger.

128
00:08:15.610 --> 00:08:18.951
"You can help the team too.

129
00:08:19.591 --> 00:08:23.617
I've been working on a move that I call a Michael Jordan Jedi Jump."

130
00:08:24.137 --> 00:08:26.698
Brooklyn jumped from side to side in front of Dirk.

131
00:08:28.899 --> 00:08:29.619
Dirk grinned.

132
00:08:29.639 --> 00:08:33.181
"Jordan will always be the king of the court.

133
00:08:33.701 --> 00:08:36.642
If Jordan were in Star Wars, he could beat Darth Vader."

134
00:08:36.662 --> 00:08:42.404
"Yep, and with this move, you might wipe that Terrier giant off the court tomorrow.

135
00:08:43.605 --> 00:08:47.166
Instead of Dirk the Jerk, you'll be Dirk the Jedi!"

136
00:08:47.827 --> 00:08:51.168
Brooklyn grabbed the ball from Dirk's hands and whipped it around her body.

137
00:08:53.561 --> 00:08:55.644
"So, do you want to give it a try?"
